Subject: [PATCH] ROADMAP 5: the plan revised by the results - judgment first,
 production later

289b came back MIND_TAPE_REAL on both holdouts with nothing trained. 1-NN
0.730 and 0.801 against a 0.333 floor; smoothness AUC 0.701 at +5.77 sigma and
0.594 at +2.51, with wrong neighbours two to five times further away than
right ones; and the number the whole plan hung on, interpolation at 0.8225 and
0.7325 against controls of 0.4575 and 0.4050. Midpoints between two same-shape
situations land on that shape. Sections 3 and 4 are not cancelled - their
precondition is measured rather than assumed.

Two caveats kept in the text because they are real. Growth saturates at an
eighth of the memory, so "the repertoire grows without retraining" is true but
plateaus early at 28 dimensions. And the labels are the three corruption ops,
not an open-ended target.

288-refuse says the thing the plan has to obey. Detection transfers across
both splits and beats counting by two and a half times on forgery and by up to
seventeen on the duplicated forgery, with clean-margin AUC at 7 and 11 sigma.
Repair is either total silence - coverage 0.000 on the corpus arm - or the
majority rule, matching votes to sixteen decimal places on the address arm.
The mind can judge and cannot yet produce.

So the order changes, because 290 asked the mind to produce values in a harder
setting than repair, with no ground truth at write time. Sending it there next
would build directly on the one measured weakness. Judgment first:
REJECT_PRESUPPOSITION, then derivations with G_depth_does_not_cost_recall
written in as it is built, then the audit sweep that turns the strongest
measured capability into an artefact. Conjecture writing waits until
production works somewhere, and the arrival index is mandatory before it.

And the result poses a question worth answering cheaply: is producing a value
hard here, or hard for this mind? 289b's memory can be asked to repair by
neighbourhood on the same subset. If the memory produces where the head does
not, the bottleneck is 6,562 weights and not the concept.

